id deep recursion (build parent, order, and children lists; then process nodes in reverse order). Use DSU-on-tree style to merge child multisets into a heavy child to keep total complexity O(n log n).\n  - Use 64-bit integers for costs (long long).\n\nThis approach matches the samples and handles the constraints (n up to 2e5) efficiently. \n\nEdge cases accounted for: if sumB != sumC -> -1; otherwise, pairing proceeds bottom-up and will either pair all mismatches or leave leftovers only if impossible (which cannot happen when sumB == sumC for a tree).\n",
